msgid ""
"If and only if the client has indicated support for twin-socket mode by "
"setting ``twin_socket.supported`` to true in its capabilities, the server "
"may optionally set up a separate command channel for server-to-client "
"commands and their replies. The server enables twin-socket mode as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:576
msgid "Create a fresh socket pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:577
msgid ""
"Keep the server end of the socket pair and pass the client end in the file "
"descriptor array included with the reply message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:579
msgid "Set ``twin_socket.supported`` to true in the reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:580
msgid ""
"Indicate the index in the file descriptor array by the "
"``twin_socket.fd_index`` capability field in the reply, so the client can "
"identify the correct file descriptor to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:584
msgid ""
"A client requesting twin-socket mode must examine the ``twin_socket`` "
"capability in the reply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:587
msgid ""
"If ``twin_socket.supported`` is false, the field is missing, or the entire "
"``twin_socket`` object is absent, the server does not support twin-socket "
"mode or decided not to enable it. The client can choose whether it wants to "
"proceed without twin-socket mode, or close the connection if not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:591
msgid ""
"If ``twin_socket.supported`` is true and ``twin_socket.fd_index`` is present "
"and refers to a valid file descriptor, twin-socket mode negotiation has "
"succeeded. The client monitors the provided file descriptor for commands "
"from the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:595
msgid ""
"Otherwise, the reply from the server is inconsistent. The client must abort "
"and close the connection since it is potentially unable to receive commands "
"from the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:599
msgid ""
"The twin-socket feature is optional, so some servers may not support it. "
"However, for server implementations that do send server-to-client commands "
"it is strongly recommended to implement twin-socket support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:606
msgid ""
"This command message is sent by the client to the server to inform it of the "
"memory regions the server can access. It must be sent before the server can "
"perform any DMA to the client. It is normally sent directly after the "
"version handshake is completed, but may also occur when memory is added to "
"the client, or if the client uses a vIOMMU."
msgstr ""

