msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1660
msgid "VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_SET"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1662
msgid "VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_PROBE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1670
msgid ""
"*flags* defines the action to be performed by the server and upon which "
"feature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1673
msgid ""
"The feature index consists of the least significant 16 bits of the flags "
"field, and can be accessed using the ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_MASK`` bit mask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1676
msgid ""
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_GET`` instructs the server to get the data for the "
"given feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1679
msgid ""
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_SET`` instructs the server to set the feature data to "
"that given in the ``data`` field of the payload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1682
msgid ""
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_PROBE`` instructs the server to probe for feature "
"support. If ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_GET`` and/or ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_SET`` "
"are also set, the probe will only return success if all of the indicated "
"methods are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1687
msgid ""
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_GET`` and ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_SET`` are mutually "
"exclusive, except for use with ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_PROBE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1690
msgid ""
"*data* is specific to the particular feature. It is not used for probing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1692
msgid ""
"This part of the request is analogous to VFIO's ``struct "
"vfio_device_feature``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1697
msgid ""
"The reply payload must be the same as the request payload for setting or "
"probing a feature. For getting a feature's data, the data is added in the "
"data section and its length is added to ``argsz``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1702
msgid "Device Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1704
msgid ""
"The only device features supported by vfio-user are those related to "
"migration, although this may change in the future. They are a subset of "
"those supported in the VFIO implementation of the Linux kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1709
msgid "Feature Index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1711
msgid "VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_MIGRATION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1713
