#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1789 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1793
msgid "(not used in vfio-user)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1791
msgid "VFIO_DEVICE_STATE_PRE_COPY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1791
msgid "The device is running normally but tracking internal state changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1793
msgid "VFIO_DEVICE_STATE_PRE_COPY_P2P"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1796
msgid ""
"*data_fd* is unused in vfio-user, as the ``VFIO_USER_MIG_DATA_READ`` and "
"``VFIO_USER_MIG_DATA_WRITE`` messages are used instead for migration data "
"transport."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1801
msgid "Direct State Transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1803
msgid ""
"The device migration FSM is a Mealy machine, so actions are taken upon the "
"arcs between FSM states. The following transitions need to be supported by "
"the server, a subset of those defined in ``<linux/vfio.h>`` (``enum "
"vfio_device_mig_state``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1808
msgid ""
"``RUNNING -> STOP``, ``STOP_COPY -> STOP``: Stop the operation of the "
"device. The ``STOP_COPY`` arc terminates the data transfer session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1811
msgid ""
"``RESUMING -> STOP``: Terminate the data transfer session. Complete "
"processing of the migration data. Stop the operation of the device. If the "
"delivered data is found to be incomplete, inconsistent, or otherwise "
"invalid, fail the ``SET`` command and optionally transition to the ``ERROR`` "
"state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1816
msgid ""
"``PRE_COPY -> RUNNING``: Terminate the data transfer session. The device is "
"now fully operational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1819
msgid "``STOP -> RUNNING``: Start the operation of the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1821
msgid ""
"``RUNNING -> PRE_COPY``, ``STOP -> STOP_COPY``: Begin the process of saving "
"the device state. The device operation is unchanged, but data transfer "
"begins. ``PRE_COPY`` and ``STOP_COPY`` are referred to as the \"saving "
"group\" of states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1826
msgid ""
"``PRE_COPY -> STOP_COPY``: Continue to transfer migration data, but stop "
"device operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1829
msgid ""
"``STOP -> RESUMING``: Start the process of restoring the device state. The "
"internal device state may be changed to prepare the device to receive the "
"migration data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1833
msgid ""
"The ``STOP_COPY -> PRE_COPY`` transition is explicitly not allowed and "
"should return an error if requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1836
msgid ""
"``ERROR`` cannot be specified as a device state, but any transition request "
"can be failed and then move the state into ``ERROR`` if the server was "
"unable to execute the requested arc AND was unable to restore the device "
"into any valid state. To recover from ``ERROR``, ``VFIO_USER_DEVICE_RESET`` "
"must be used to return back to ``RUNNING``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1842
msgid "If ``PRE_COPY`` is not supported, arcs touching it are removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1845
msgid "Complex State Transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1847
msgid ""
"The remaining possible transitions are to be implemented as combinations of "
"the above FSM arcs. As there are multiple paths, the path should be selected "
"based on the following rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1851
msgid "Select the shortest path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1853
msgid ""
"The path cannot have saving group states as interior arcs, only start/end "
"states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1857
msgid ""
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_DMA_LOGGING_START`` / "
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_DMA_LOGGING_STOP``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1859
msgid ""
"Upon ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_SET``, start/stop DMA logging. These features can "
"also be probed to determine whether the device supports DMA logging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1862
msgid ""
"When DMA logging is started, a range of IOVAs to monitor is provided and the "
"device can optimize its logging to cover only the IOVA range given. Only DMA "
"writes are logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1866
msgid "The data field of the ``SET`` request is structured as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1871 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1921
msgid "page_size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1873
msgid "num_ranges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1877
msgid "ranges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1880
msgid ""
"*page_size* hints what tracking granularity the device should try to "
"achieve. If the device cannot do the hinted page size then it's the driver's "
"choice which page size to pick based on its support. On output the device "
"will return the page size it selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1885
msgid ""
"*num_ranges* is the number of IOVA ranges to monitor. A value of zero "
"indicates that all writes should be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1888
msgid ""
"*ranges* is an array of ``vfio_user_device_feature_dma_logging_range`` "
"entries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1894 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1917
msgid "iova"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1896 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1919
msgid "length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1899 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1924
msgid "*iova* is the base IO virtual address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1900
msgid "*length* is the length of the range to log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1902
msgid ""
"Upon success, the response data field will be the same as the request, "
"unless the page size was changed, in which case this will be reflected in "
"the response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1906
msgid "``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_DMA_LOGGING_REPORT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1908
msgid ""
"Upon ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_GET``, returns the dirty bitmap for a specific "
"IOVA range. This operation is only valid if logging of dirty pages has been "
"previously started by setting ``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_DMA_LOGGING_START``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1912
msgid "The data field of the request is structured as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1926
msgid "*length* is the length of the range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1928
msgid ""
"*page_size* is the unit of granularity of the bitmap, and must be a power of "
"two. It doesn't have to match the value given to "
"``VFIO_DEVICE_FEATURE_DMA_LOGGING_START`` because the driver will format its "
"internal logging to match the reporting page size possibly by replicating "
"bits if the internal page size is lower than requested"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1934
msgid ""
"The data field of the response is identical, except with the bitmap added on "
"the end at offset 24."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1937
msgid ""
"The bitmap is an array of u64s that holds the output bitmap, with 1 bit "
"reporting a *page_size* unit of IOVA. The bits outside of the requested "
"range must be zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1941
msgid "The mapping of IOVA to bits is given by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1943
msgid "``bitmap[(addr - iova)/page_size] & (1ULL << (addr % 64))``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1948
msgid ""
"This command is used to read data from the source migration server while it "
"is in a saving group state (``PRE_COPY`` or ``STOP_COPY``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1951
msgid ""
"This command, and ``VFIO_USER_MIG_DATA_WRITE``, are used in place of the "
"``data_fd`` file descriptor in ``<linux/vfio.h>`` (``struct "
"vfio_device_feature_mig_state``) to enable all data transport to use the "
"single already-established UNIX socket. Hence, the migration data is treated "
"like a stream, so the client must continue reading until no more migration "
"data remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1973
msgid "*size* is the size of the migration data to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1978
msgid ""
"The reply payload for this message is a structure of the following format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1990
msgid ""
"*argsz* is the size of the above structure, including the size of the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1992
msgid ""
"*size* indicates the size of returned migration data. If this is less than "
"the requested size, there is no more migration data to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:1995 ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:2025
msgid "*data* contains the migration data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:2000
msgid ""
"This command is used to write data to the destination migration server while "
"it is in the ``RESUMING`` state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:2003
msgid ""
"As above, this replaces the ``data_fd`` file descriptor for transport of "
"migration data, and as such, the migration data is treated like a stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:2023
msgid "*size* is the size of the migration data to be written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../interop/vfio-user.rst:2030
msgid "There is no reply payload for this message."
msgstr ""

